window.PLACEHOLDER_CSV = "id,direction,source,reference,conversation_id,context\nITEM_001,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我想从我的账户上取些钱。\n\n[Turn 2] 我能看看你的存折和取款单吗？\n\n[Turn 3] 好的。\n\n[Turn 4] 我需要确定一下，你想取一千美元吗？\n\n[Turn 5] 没错。\",\"[Turn 1] I'd like to withdraw some money from my account .\n\n[Turn 2] Can I see your passbook and the withdrawal slip , please ?\n\n[Turn 3] Sure .\n\n[Turn 4] Let me just make sure . You want to withdraw one thousand dollars ?\n\n[Turn 5] That's right .\",CONV_001,\nITEM_002,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 下面有一个倒过来的小迪尔伯特\n\n[Turn 2] 当你翻开领带时，他是正面朝上的。太棒了\n\n[Turn 3] 我爸爸肯定会喜欢，他是迪尔伯特的粉丝。\n\n[Turn 4] 我自己也想买一个...\n\n[Turn 5] 给我做个模型\n\n[Turn 6] 好的！\n\n[Turn 7] 哇！你看起来和迪尔伯特一样，傻乎乎的！\",\"[Turn 1] And there's a little upside-down Dilbert on the underside .\n\n[Turn 2] When you flip the tie up , he's right side up . Brilliant .\n\n[Turn 3] My dad will love this . He's a Dilbert fan .\n\n[Turn 4] I wouldn't mind having one myself ...\n\n[Turn 5] Model it for me .\n\n[Turn 6] OK !\n\n[Turn 7] Wow ! You look just as dorky as Dilbert !\",CONV_002,\nITEM_003,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 你经常看电视吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 不怎么看。我看不看无所谓。\n\n[Turn 3] 我就不行。我必须要看电视，任何节目都行。\n\n[Turn 4] 你是怎么做到的？\",\"[Turn 1] Do you watch TV a lot?\n\n[Turn 2] Not really. I don’t really care whether I watch it or not.\n\n[Turn 3] I’m not like that. I have to watch TV—anything will do.\n\n[Turn 4] How do you do that?\",CONV_003,\nITEM_004,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] May I ask a question ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , what's it ?\n\n[Turn 3] What does mph stand for ?\n\n[Turn 4] It's miles per hour .\",\"[Turn 1] 我可以问个问题吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 可以，问题是什么？\n\n[Turn 3] mph是什么意思？\n\n[Turn 4] 每小时多少英里。\",CONV_004,\nITEM_005,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 今晚去看电影怎么样？\n\n[Turn 2] 太好了。今晚有什么电影？\n\n[Turn 3] 我不确定这部电影的名字，但我知道它很浪漫。\n\n[Turn 4] 浪漫？但是我更喜欢惊悚片。\n\n[Turn 5] 你不觉得惊悚片太血腥了吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 恰恰相反，它让我兴奋。\",\"[Turn 1] How about going to see a movie tonight?\n\n[Turn 2] Sounds great. What's playing tonight?\n\n[Turn 3] I'm not sure what the movie's called, but I know it's really romantic.\n\n[Turn 4] Romantic? But I prefer thrillers.\n\n[Turn 5] Don't you think thrillers are too bloody?\n\n[Turn 6] Just the opposite. They get me excited.\",CONV_005,\nITEM_006,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 玛丽，很高兴见到你。\n\n[Turn 2] 我和约什刚从海滩回家，想顺便过来看看。\n\n[Turn 3] 很高兴见到你们。\n\n[Turn 4] 对，我们很久都没见到你。\n\n[Turn 5] 玛丽，我给乔希或你拿点喝的吧。\n\n[Turn 6] 哦，不，谢谢。我们并不渴。\n\n[Turn 7] 那么来点吃的怎么样。\n\n[Turn 8] 不，谢谢，我们刚吃过午饭。\n\n[Turn 9] 那么，你的家人好吗？\n\n[Turn 10] 每个人都很好。我妹妹终于有自己的孩子了。\",\"[Turn 1] Mary, it's so good to see you.\n\n[Turn 2] Josh and I just got back from the beach, and we thought we'd stop by.\n\n[Turn 3] It's great to see you both.\n\n[Turn 4] Yeah, we haven't seen you in ages.\n\n[Turn 5] Mary, can I get Josh or you something to drink?\n\n[Turn 6] Oh, no, thanks. We're not thirsty.\n\n[Turn 7] Well, how about something to eat?\n\n[Turn 8] No, thanks. We just had lunch.\n\n[Turn 9] So, how's your family?\n\n[Turn 10] Everyone's doing well. My sister finally has a child of her own.\",CONV_006,\nITEM_007,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] So , basically ,\n\n[Turn 2] if you hold it like that , the one on your thumb , yeah , [vocalsound:other] the thumb button is the power button .\n\n[Turn 3] Mm-hmm .\n\n[Turn 4] Mm-hmm .\",\"[Turn 1] 所以，基本上，\n\n[Turn 2] 你要是那样拿着它，拇指那边那个，对，[声音:其他] 那个拇指键就是电源键。\n\n[Turn 3] 嗯哼。\n\n[Turn 4] 嗯哼。\",CONV_007,\nITEM_008,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] I saw a rat in my house and now I'm worried it will contaminate my food and make me sick.\n\n[Turn 2] Well, rats are known to carry diseases, so it's definitely possible that it could make you sick. But if you take some precautions, like washing your hands thoroughly after coming into contact with anything the rat may have touched, you should be okay.\n\n[Turn 3] I'm not sure if I can trust myself to be that careful. Do you think I should call an exterminator?\n\n[Turn 4] If you're really worried about it, then yeah, maybe calling an exterminator would be a good idea.\n\n[Turn 5] But what if they use harsh chemicals that are even more dangerous than the rat?\n\n[Turn 6] You could always ask them to use natural, eco-friendly products instead.\",\"[Turn 1] 我在家里看见一只老鼠，现在很担心它会把我的食物弄脏，害我生病。\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，老鼠确实会携带疾病，所以它让你生病也不是没可能。不过你只要做好点防护，比如碰过任何老鼠可能碰到的东西之后，把手彻底洗干净，应该就没事。\n\n[Turn 3] 我不确定自己能不能做到那么小心。你觉得我该叫灭鼠公司吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 如果你真的很担心，那嗯，也许叫灭鼠公司来会比较好。\n\n[Turn 5] 可是万一他们用那种很刺激的化学药剂，比老鼠还危险怎么办？\n\n[Turn 6] 你也可以让他们改用天然、环保的产品啊。\",CONV_008,\nITEM_009,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 你看看你需要需要，你落，需要你去跑的去落实的这些，如果你呢。\n\n[Turn 2] 呃，干不过来，你再找。\n\n[Turn 3] 啊，再找派几个人一起，比较好。\n\n[Turn 4] 再派几个人一起去吧，嗯，比较好，嗯，对。\n\n[Turn 5] 啊一起啊啊啊。\n\n[Turn 6] 第一步呢。\n\n[Turn 7] 第一步先去落实商场的费用问题。\n\n[Turn 8] 和商场的这个。\",\"[Turn 1] Take a look at what you need—what needs you to go out and follow up on—if you... you know.\n\n[Turn 2] Uh, if you can't handle it all, then find some more people.\n\n[Turn 3] Yeah, get a few more people to go with you. That’d be better.\n\n[Turn 4] Yeah, send a few more people to go together. Mm, that’d be better. Mm, right.\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah, together, yeah, yeah, yeah.\n\n[Turn 6] The first step is...\n\n[Turn 7] First, go and sort out the issue of the mall fees.\n\n[Turn 8] And the mall’s, uh...\",CONV_009,\nITEM_010,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 而且双十一不敢买就是买完以后你不知道什么时候才能收到货，等半天。\n\n[Turn 2] 还一个就是双十一的这个退货哈，其实他是一个很，很繁琐的一个过程，因为客服他一，势必要对接很多人的退货。\n\n[Turn 3] 率很高。\",\"[Turn 1] And another reason I don’t dare buy stuff on Double Eleven is that after you place the order, you have no idea when it’ll actually arrive. You end up waiting forever.\n\n[Turn 2] Another thing is returns during Double Eleven. Honestly, it’s a really, really cumbersome process, because customer service is inevitably dealing with tons of people’s returns.\n\n[Turn 3] The return rate is really high.\",CONV_010,\nITEM_011,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 下一位！您好，先生，能为您做什么吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，我要寄一封航空挂号信到法国。\n\n[Turn 3] 好的，四美元二十美分。\n\n[Turn 4] 这是五美元。\n\n[Turn 5] 这是您的零钱，请等一下您的挂号收据。\n\n[Turn 6] 我还想取包裹，这是通知单。\n\n[Turn 7] 让我看一看。嗯，等一会，给您，我们需要您在这张票据上签名。\n\n[Turn 8] 哦，还有一件事，我在哪儿投这封信？\n\n[Turn 9] 把它投进那个角落里标有“外埠”的邮箱。\n\n[Turn 10] 非常感谢\n\n[Turn 11] 不客气。\",\"[Turn 1] Next! Hello, sir. What can I do for you?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes, I’d like to send this by registered airmail to France.\n\n[Turn 3] Sure. That’ll be four dollars and twenty cents.\n\n[Turn 4] Here’s five dollars.\n\n[Turn 5] Here’s your change. Please wait a moment for your registered mail receipt.\n\n[Turn 6] I’d also like to pick up a package. Here’s the notice.\n\n[Turn 7] Let me take a look. Hmm, just a moment. Here you go. We’ll need you to sign this slip.\n\n[Turn 8] Oh, one more thing—where do I mail this letter?\n\n[Turn 9] Drop it in the mailbox in the corner marked “Out of Town.”\n\n[Turn 10] Thank you very much.\n\n[Turn 11] You’re welcome.\",CONV_011,\nITEM_012,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] N We've gonna [disfmarker:] We're going to evaluate it .\n\n[Turn 2] We're gonna go to our other room again .\n\n[Turn 3] Well , anyhow . These are seven factors times seven is forty\n\n[Turn 4] something . Two ?\n\n[Turn 5] No . Nine ?\n\n[Turn 6] [gap:] Forty nine .\n\n[Turn 7] Uh , minus one .\n\n[Turn 8] Minus three , minus four . [vocalsound:prosodic repetition vocalisation]\",\"[Turn 1] 嗯，我们要……我们会来评估一下。\n\n[Turn 2] 我们还要再去另一个房间。\n\n[Turn 3] 哎，反正吧。这是七个因素乘以七，是四十\n\n[Turn 4] 几来着。二？\n\n[Turn 5] 不对。九？\n\n[Turn 6] 四十九。\n\n[Turn 7] 呃，减一。\n\n[Turn 8] 减三，减四。嗯嗯嗯。\",CONV_012,\nITEM_013,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Man , I'm hungry . Do you know a good place to have lunch ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , I know a great place . What types of food do you like ?\n\n[Turn 3] Mexican , Japanese or Chinese would be great .\n\n[Turn 4] Oh , I know a place where you might like to eat .\n\n[Turn 5] Is it close by ?\n\n[Turn 6] It's down a block on the right ; can I show you the way ?\n\n[Turn 7] OK , I'd love the company .\n\n[Turn 8] This will work out well . I'm getting hungry just thinking about it .\",\"[Turn 1] 伙计，我饿了。你知道什么吃午饭的好地方吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，我知道一个很棒的地方。你喜欢什么类型的食物？\n\n[Turn 3] 墨西哥菜、日本菜或中国菜都可以。\n\n[Turn 4] 哦，我知道一个地方你可能喜欢吃。\n\n[Turn 5] 离这儿近吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 在右边一个街区的尽头；我能给你带路，好吗？\n\n[Turn 7] 好的，我喜欢有人陪。\n\n[Turn 8] 这家餐厅会很好吃的。一想到我就饿了。\",CONV_013,\nITEM_014,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] I'm so excited to be married to a Klingon! I've always been attracted to your culture and way of life.\n\n[Turn 2] Yes, our culture is very different from yours. But I think that's one of the things that drew you to me.\n\n[Turn 3] I know it won't be easy, but I'm willing to learn about your culture and make compromises. I just want our family to be happy and thrive.\n\n[Turn 4] That's very important to me too. I want us to be able to share our cultures with each other and our children. It will be a challenge, but I think we can do it if we're open-minded and patient with each other.\n\n[Turn 5] I'm definitely open to that. I think it will be a great experience for our family. Thanks for being understanding and supportive.\n\n[Turn 6] Of course. I love you, Reagen.\",\"[Turn 1] 能嫁给一个克林贡人，我真的太兴奋了！我一直都很被你们的文化和生活方式吸引。\n\n[Turn 2] 是啊，我们的文化跟你们很不一样。但我想，这也是你被我吸引的原因之一吧。\n\n[Turn 3] 我知道这不会容易，但我愿意去了解你的文化，也愿意做出妥协。我只希望我们的家庭能幸福、兴旺。\n\n[Turn 4] 这对我也非常重要。我希望我们能彼此分享各自的文化，也分享给我们的孩子。会有挑战，但我相信只要我们都保持开放的心态，对彼此有耐心，我们就能做到。\n\n[Turn 5] 我当然愿意。我觉得这对我们一家来说会是一次很棒的经历。谢谢你这么理解我、支持我。\n\n[Turn 6] 当然了。我爱你，Reagen。\",CONV_014,\nITEM_015,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 这些一些。\n\n[Turn 2] 该用的一些小礼品或者一些场景，我们。\n\n[Turn 3] 还有吧。\n\n[Turn 4] 呃，需要去找一下，在库房如果不够的话还是需要补，因为是传统文化嘛。\n\n[Turn 5] 所以说。\n\n[Turn 6] 呃，之前的活动的话，没有这方面的重叠。\",\"[Turn 1] Some of these things.\n\n[Turn 2] The little gifts we need to use, or some of the setups, we...\n\n[Turn 3] There are more, right?\n\n[Turn 4] Uh, we need to go check. If there isn’t enough in the storeroom, we’ll still need to restock, since it’s traditional culture and all.\n\n[Turn 5] So...\n\n[Turn 6] Uh, the previous events didn’t really overlap in this area.\",CONV_015,\nITEM_016,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] No , but but I think uh de\n\n[Turn 2] Except the switchboard .\",\"[Turn 1] 没有，不过，不过我觉得呃，那个……\n\n[Turn 2] 除了总机。\",CONV_016,\nITEM_017,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 早上好。我是布朗先生。我来自澳大利亚。这是我的名片。\n\n[Turn 2] 非常感谢。很高兴见到你，布朗先生。我叫凯西·皮尔斯，是格林纺织品进出口公司的代表。\n\n[Turn 3] 我也很高兴见到你，皮尔斯女士。我每年都出差，但这是我第一次来贵国。我必须说你们友好的人民给我留下了深刻的印象。\n\n[Turn 4] 谢谢你这么说。你看过展览馆吗？展出的是我们的大部分产品，如丝绸、毛织品、棉布和服装。\n\n[Turn 5] 哦，是的。我昨天看了一眼。我发现有些展品质量很好，设计也很漂亮。展览会成功地向我展示了贵公司的业务。我已经看了你上封信所附的目录和小册子。我对你们的出口产品有了些了解。我对你们的丝绸衬衫也很感兴趣。\n\n[Turn 6] 我们的丝绸以质量好而闻名。这是我们贸易出口的产品之一。丝绸衬衫色彩鲜艳，设计精美。他们在海外受到了很大的青睐，需求量一直很大。\",\"[Turn 1] Good morning . My name is Mr . Brown . I ’ m from Australia . Here is my card .\n\n[Turn 2] Thank you . I ’ m pleased to meet you , Mr . Brown . My name is Kathy Pewless , the representative of Green Textile Import and Export Corporation .\n\n[Turn 3] Pleased to meet you too , Ms . Pewless . I travel a lot every year on business , but this is my first visit to your country . I must say I have been much impressed by your friendly people .\n\n[Turn 4] Thank you for saying so . Have you seen the exhibition halls ? On display are most of our products , such as silk , woolen knitwear , cotton piece goods , and garments .\n\n[Turn 5] Oh , yes . I had a look yesterday . I found some of the exhibits to be fine in quality and beautiful in design . The exhibition has successfully displayed to me what your corporation handles . I ’ Ve gone over the catalogue and the pamphlets enclosed in your last letter . I ’ Ve got some idea of your exports . I ’ m interested in your silk blouses .\n\n[Turn 6] Our silk is known for its good quality . It is one of our trade - trional exports . Silk blouses are brightly colored and beau - fully designed . They ’ Ve met with great favor overseas and are always in great demand .\",CONV_017,\nITEM_018,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] I'm just not sure what I'm supposed to be doing with my life. I feel like I'm just floating through it without any real purpose.\n\n[Turn 2] That sounds pretty tough. Do you have any ideas of what you might want to do?\n\n[Turn 3] Yeah, I've been thinking about going back to school. But then I think about how much debt I'll be in and it doesn't seem worth it.\n\n[Turn 4] Have you talked to anyone about this? A guidance counselor or anyone?\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah, a few people actually. They all say the same thing basically. That I should follow my heart and do what makes me happy. But how am I supposed to know what that is? And even if I did know, how am I supposed to make it happen? It all just seems so impossible.\n\n[Turn 6] Well, first of all, you're not alone in feeling like this. A lot of people go through life without really knowing what they want to do with their lives. As for making your dreams come true, that's definitely possible but it's going to take some hard work and dedication. You have to believe in yourself and have faith that things will work out the way you want them too. Just take things one step at a time and don't get too ahead of yourself. And most importantly, don't give up on your dreams!\n\n[Turn 7] Yeah, I guess you're right. Thanks for listening. It really helps to talk to someone about this stuff.\n\n[Turn 8] No problem, anytime!\",\"[Turn 1] 我就是不太确定自己这辈子到底该做什么。感觉自己一直就这么飘着，没什么真正的目标。\n\n[Turn 2] 听起来挺难受的。那你有没有想过自己可能想做什么？\n\n[Turn 3] 有啊，我一直在想要不要回去上学。但一想到会背上那么多债，就觉得好像不太值。\n\n[Turn 4] 你有跟别人聊过这件事吗？比如升学顾问之类的人？\n\n[Turn 5] 有，其实聊过几个人。他们基本上都说一样的话，说我应该跟着自己的心走，做让我开心的事。可我怎么知道那到底是什么呢？就算我知道了，我又该怎么把它实现呢？这一切都感觉太不可能了。\n\n[Turn 6] 嗯，首先，有这种感觉的不只你一个。很多人过一辈子，其实也不太清楚自己到底想做什么。至于让梦想成真，那当然是有可能的，只是需要付出很多努力，也要坚持。你得相信自己，也要相信事情会朝着你希望的方向发展。一步一步来，别一下子想太远。最重要的是，别放弃你的梦想！\n\n[Turn 7] 嗯，我想你说得对。谢谢你愿意听我说。能跟人聊聊这些事，真的挺有帮助的。\n\n[Turn 8] 没事，随时都可以！\",CONV_018,\nITEM_019,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我昨天和大卫大吵了一架。我希望他现在不生我的气了。\n\n[Turn 2] 你们在吵什么？\n\n[Turn 3] 他向我借了一些钱，我需要要回来。他说他还没有钱。\n\n[Turn 4] 他应该还你钱。这很合理。\n\n[Turn 5] 是的，但是我很快就生他的气了。他可能认为我不信任他。我不该生气的。\n\n[Turn 6] 你借给他很多钱了吗？\n\n[Turn 7] 不多。但我突然要付一笔钱，所以我需要找他要钱。\n\n[Turn 8] 好吧，下次你见到他时跟他谈谈。他可能和你一样难过。亲密的朋友有时会有分歧。这很寻常。你们两个都没说什么难听的话吧？\n\n[Turn 9] 不，我们都没有。我想你是对的。我们应该修补一下关系。\n\n[Turn 10] 你当然应该。你不会希望一场愚蠢的争吵毁掉一段长久的友谊吧？\",\"[Turn 1] I had a huge fight with David yesterday. I hope he’s not mad at me anymore.\n\n[Turn 2] What were you two arguing about?\n\n[Turn 3] He borrowed some money from me, and I needed it back. He said he didn’t have the money yet.\n\n[Turn 4] He should pay you back. That’s fair.\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah, but I got angry with him pretty quickly. He probably thought I didn’t trust him. I shouldn’t have gotten mad.\n\n[Turn 6] Did you lend him a lot of money?\n\n[Turn 7] Not much. But I suddenly had a payment to make, so I needed to ask him for the money.\n\n[Turn 8] Well, talk to him the next time you see him. He might be just as upset as you are. Close friends have disagreements sometimes. It’s totally normal. Neither of you said anything hurtful, did you?\n\n[Turn 9] No, neither of us did. I think you’re right. We should patch things up.\n\n[Turn 10] You definitely should. You don’t want one stupid argument to ruin a long friendship, do you?\",CONV_019,\nITEM_020,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我，天猫有呀。\n\n[Turn 2] 天猫也有嘛，那就是嘛，那，那就是阿里下边儿都有嘛，京东没有是吧？\n\n[Turn 3] 因为我觉得天猫就和和和那个。\n\n[Turn 4] 京东没有。\",\"[Turn 1] I mean, Tmall has it.\n\n[Turn 2] Tmall has it too? Right, so that means everything under Alibaba has it, then. JD doesn’t, right?\n\n[Turn 3] Because I feel like Tmall is just like, like, like that...\n\n[Turn 4] JD doesn’t have it.\",CONV_020,\nITEM_021,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] They got a divorce at last .\n\n[Turn 2] It's inevitable . Their love wasbuilt on the sand , and this is why their marriage has landed on the rocks .\n\n[Turn 3] You said it . Love but on the sand will soon be on the rocks .\n\n[Turn 4] That give us a good lesson .\",\"[Turn 1] 他们最后还是离婚了。\n\n[Turn 2] 这是迟早的事。他们的爱情本来就像建在沙子上一样不牢靠，所以婚姻才会触礁。\n\n[Turn 3] 你说得对。建在沙子上的爱情，很快就会触礁。\n\n[Turn 4] 这也给了我们一个很好的教训。\",CONV_021,\nITEM_022,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Now um [vocalsound:other] we have to get down to the nitty-gritty of how to make this and this remote control has to be sold [disfmarker:] um we're to sell it for twenty five Euros , with a profit aim ultimately of fifty million Euros . That tells you something about how many um we have to sell on an international scale . Um would be an awful lot of these , would be like what , a hundred million of them um to make twenty five Euros on each one and to make a total profit of fifty million . Um the production is to only cost twelve and a half Euros per item .\n\n[Turn 2] Now if they cost twelve and a half , you're selling it for twenty five , you're making twelve and a half Euros each . Um and we're to make a profit of fifty million , that's t uh [disfmarker:] can you do the maths and how many are we selling ?\n\n[Turn 3] [vocalsound:other] Uh yeah . [vocalsound:other] I was just wondering if that's the um [disfmarker:]\n\n[Turn 4] If fifty percent is normal [disfmarker:]\",\"[Turn 1] 那现在，嗯，（发声）我们得具体说说这东西要怎么做了，而且这个遥控器得卖出去，呃，我们要卖二十五欧元，最终的利润目标是五千万欧元。这就能看出来，我们在国际范围内得卖多少个。嗯，这种东西得卖特别多，大概是多少，一亿个吧，嗯，每个赚二十五欧元，总利润做到五千万。嗯，生产成本每件只能是十二点五欧元。\n\n[Turn 2] 那如果成本是十二点五，卖二十五，那每个就赚十二点五欧元。嗯，我们要赚五千万，那就是，呃，你能算一下吗，我们到底要卖多少个？\n\n[Turn 3] （发声）呃，对。（发声）我刚才就在想，这个是不是那个，呃……\n\n[Turn 4] 如果百分之五十算正常的话，呃……\",CONV_022,\nITEM_023,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Hi, Sally. It's been a while since we talked.\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah, I know. I'm sorry I've been so busy lately.\n\n[Turn 3] That's okay. I understand. So what have you been up to?\n\n[Turn 4] Oh, you know, just the usual stuff. work, school, hanging out with friends. Nothing exciting.\n\n[Turn 5] That sounds like a lot more fun than what I've been doing lately. \u0010I've just been working and studying all the time lately and it's getting pretty boring.\n\n[Turn 6] Yeah, I can imagine that would be pretty boring after a while. You should try to do something fun once in awhile to break up the monotony. \u0010Maybe go out with some friends or go on a trip or something like that.\n\n[Turn 7] Yeah, that's a good idea. I'll definitely try to do that more often from now on. Thanks for the advice, Sally!\",\"[Turn 1] 嗨，Sally。我们好久没聊了。\n\n[Turn 2] 是啊，我知道。不好意思，我最近一直特别忙。\n\n[Turn 3] 没事，我理解。那你最近都忙什么呢？\n\n[Turn 4] 哦，你也知道，就那些平常的事。工作、上学、跟朋友出去玩。没什么特别刺激的。\n\n[Turn 5] 听起来可比我最近做的事有意思多了。我最近就是一直工作、学习，真的越来越无聊了。\n\n[Turn 6] 是啊，我能想象，时间一长肯定挺无聊的。你应该偶尔做点好玩的事，换换心情。比如跟朋友出去玩，或者去旅行什么的。\n\n[Turn 7] 嗯，是个好主意。从现在开始我一定会尽量多这么做的。谢谢你的建议，Sally！\",CONV_023,\nITEM_024,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 需要我帮忙吗\n\n[Turn 2] 是的。你们这里可以兑换外币吗？\n\n[Turn 3] 是的。我行被授权办理外汇业务。\n\n[Turn 4] 你们可以兑换哪种货币？\n\n[Turn 5] 我们只能兑换三种货币，美元、日元和港币。\n\n[Turn 6] 你能告诉我今天美元的兑换率是多少吗？\n\n[Turn 7] 买入价是826。100美元兑换44元。\n\n[Turn 8] 我想兑换一些美元来支付我在这里的费用。\n\n[Turn 9] 请到2号外汇柜台。在那边。\n\n[Turn 10] 谢谢你\",\"[Turn 1] Do you need any help?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes. Can I exchange foreign currency here?\n\n[Turn 3] Yes. Our bank is authorized to handle foreign exchange.\n\n[Turn 4] What currencies can you exchange?\n\n[Turn 5] We can only exchange three currencies: U.S. dollars, Japanese yen, and Hong Kong dollars.\n\n[Turn 6] Can you tell me today’s exchange rate for U.S. dollars?\n\n[Turn 7] The buying rate is 826. One hundred U.S. dollars exchanges for 44 yuan.\n\n[Turn 8] I’d like to exchange some U.S. dollars to cover my expenses here.\n\n[Turn 9] Please go to foreign exchange counter number 2. It’s over there.\n\n[Turn 10] Thank you.\",CONV_024,\nITEM_025,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Like zapping is just switching one channel at a time .\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah , maybe it's not easy if it's below . It's harder to zap . So I think uh it should be\n\n[Turn 3] should be easy to [gap:] .\n\n[Turn 4] I think it's pretty standard , these rubber buttons on the top .\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah okay . That's that's good , but [disfmarker:]\n\n[Turn 6] And uh if you don't light 'em up , they don't uh [vocalsound:other] you don't see 'em very good . [vocalsound:other] I think it's modern to light this area up , and to light this area up . So the focus gets on these parts and not on there .\",\"[Turn 1] 就像换台嘛，就是一次切一个频道。\n\n[Turn 2] 对，可能如果在下面的话就不太方便。换台会更费劲。所以我觉得呃，应该要\n\n[Turn 3] 应该要很容易[gap:]。\n\n[Turn 4] 我觉得上面这些橡胶按键挺标准的。\n\n[Turn 5] 嗯，好。这个挺好，不过[disfmarker:]\n\n[Turn 6] 还有呃，如果不把它们点亮，就呃[vocalsound:other]看不太清楚。[vocalsound:other]我觉得把这一区域点亮、还有这一区域点亮，会比较现代。这样注意力就会集中在这些部分，而不是那边。\",CONV_025,\nITEM_026,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Lillie, I don't know what to say. Your kindness is so overwhelming. I feel like I'm about to cry.\n\n[Turn 2] Oh, don't cry Alexandria. I'm just glad I could help you in some way.\n\n[Turn 3] It's just that, I've never experienced anything like this before. This feeling of love and compassion is so new to me.\n\n[Turn 4] Then let's savor it and enjoy it while it lasts!\n\n[Turn 5] You're right. I'm sorry for getting emotional.\n\n[Turn 6] There's nothing to be sorry about. This is a beautiful moment that we're sharing.\",\"[Turn 1] Lillie，我都不知道该说什么了。你对我这么好，真的让我受宠若惊。我感觉自己都快哭了。\n\n[Turn 2] 哎呀，别哭，Alexandria。我只是很高兴能帮上你一点忙。\n\n[Turn 3] 只是……我以前从来没经历过这样的事。这种被爱、被关怀的感觉，对我来说太陌生了。\n\n[Turn 4] 那我们就好好感受它，趁现在尽情享受吧！\n\n[Turn 5] 你说得对。抱歉，我有点太激动了。\n\n[Turn 6] 没什么好抱歉的。这是属于我们一起分享的美好时刻。\",CONV_026,\nITEM_027,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] I can't stand it when things don't go my way. I'm always trying to control everything and everyone around me.\n\n[Turn 2] That must be really tough for you. I can imagine how frustrating it must be when you can't control everything.\n\n[Turn 3] It is! I feel like I have to be in charge all the time, and it's just exhausting. I wish things would just go my way for once, but it seems like that's never going to happen.\n\n[Turn 4] Well, maybe you can try relaxing a bit and see if that helps? Sometimes letting go of the need to control everything can be helpful.\n\n[Turn 5] I don't know...I feel like if I relax, then things will just spiral out of control. I don't know how to let go and not worry about everything all the time.\n\n[Turn 6] Maybe there's a middle ground somewhere? Where you're not so stressed out all the time, but still able to maintain some level of control? It might take some trial and error to find what works for you, but it's worth a shot!\",\"[Turn 1] 事情不按我的意思来，我就受不了。我总是想控制身边所有事、所有人。\n\n[Turn 2] 那对你来说肯定挺难受的。我能想象，没法掌控一切的时候会有多烦。\n\n[Turn 3] 就是啊！我感觉自己必须一直掌控局面，真的太累了。我真希望事情能哪怕一次按我的意思来，可好像永远都不会发生。\n\n[Turn 4] 嗯，也许你可以试着放松一点，看看会不会有帮助？有时候，放下那种必须控制一切的念头，反而会好一些。\n\n[Turn 5] 我不知道……我感觉我要是一放松，事情就会彻底失控。我不知道怎么放手，也不知道怎么不一直为所有事担心。\n\n[Turn 6] 也许可以找个折中的办法？既不用一直这么紧绷，又还能保持一定程度的掌控。可能得试几次才知道什么适合你，但值得试试！\",CONV_027,\nITEM_028,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 啊，对嗯。\n\n[Turn 2] 现在冰箱。\n\n[Turn 3] 挺不错都是，但是现在是唯一缺什么你知道吗？以后再进步有一个，就是智智能化能不能，那个检验检验那个农残的问题，你知道吧。\n\n[Turn 4] 好的。\n\n[Turn 5] 最好最好是在冰箱儿是吧，完了把那个菜放里边儿以后，完了通通过面板儿显示，这通过老年人那会儿或者这一看呢，就能看出来。\n\n[Turn 6] 对，他这个。\",\"[Turn 1] Ah, right, mm-hmm.\n\n[Turn 2] Fridges these days...\n\n[Turn 3] They're all pretty good, but you know the one thing they're still missing? For future improvement, it would be whether the smart features can, you know, test for pesticide residue. You know what I mean?\n\n[Turn 4] Got it.\n\n[Turn 5] Ideally, with the fridge, right, after you put the vegetables inside, it would show it on the panel, so older people—or anyone, really—could tell just by looking.\n\n[Turn 6] Right, this one...\",CONV_028,\nITEM_029,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Honey , I need to have a talk with you .\n\n[Turn 2] Dad , I have to do my homework .\n\n[Turn 3] No , honey , why didn't you go to cram school last night ?\n\n[Turn 4] Dad , I don't want to talk about it now .\n\n[Turn 5] Honey , if you don't want to go to cram school , you should tell me the reason why .\n\n[Turn 6] I'm sorry , dad . But I would rather stay at school than go to cram school .\",\"[Turn 1] 亲爱的，我需要和你谈谈。\n\n[Turn 2] 爸爸，我得做作业。\n\n[Turn 3] 不，亲爱的，你昨晚为什么没去补习班？\n\n[Turn 4] 爸爸，我现在不想谈这个。\n\n[Turn 5] 亲爱的，如果你不想去补习班，你应该告诉我原因。\n\n[Turn 6] 对不起，爸爸。但我宁愿留在学校也不愿去补习班。\",CONV_029,\nITEM_030,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Excuse me . Is this where I catch the bus for the zoo ?\n\n[Turn 2] Well , you can take the No . 36 bus from here , but then you have to walk about 30 minutes .\n\n[Turn 3] That doesn't sound too bad .\n\n[Turn 4] Actually , if you go to the bus stop in the next block , you can take bus 301 which will let you right off in front of the zoo .\n\n[Turn 5] Maybe that's what I'll do . Thanks a lot .\n\n[Turn 6] You're welcome .\",\"[Turn 1] 不好意思，请问是在这儿坐去动物园的公交吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，你可以在这儿坐36路，不过下车后还得走大概30分钟。\n\n[Turn 3] 听起来也还行。\n\n[Turn 4] 其实，你要是去下一个街区的公交站，可以坐301路，直接在动物园门口下。\n\n[Turn 5] 那我可能就这么走吧。太谢谢了。\n\n[Turn 6] 不客气。\",CONV_030,\nITEM_031,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Good afternoon ! Did you call for a plumber ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , yes I did . Please come in ! I ’ m so glad you came ! This old house is falling apart ! Come on into the bathroom . See , here , there ’ s water leaking everywhere !\n\n[Turn 3] I see . Let me have a look . It seems that your toilet is clogged , and that ’ s why it won ’ t flush . Let me just get my plunger . No , that ’ s not working either . I suspect that there ’ s some sort of foreign object in the pipes that ‘ s causing a blockage . That ’ s what ’ s making your toilet overflow .\n\n[Turn 4] Oh , that must be because of my four-year-old daughter . She is always flushing things down the toilet . You know how kids are .\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah , I have a little one myself . Anyway , these water pipes are really rusty , so they also should be changed . Thatcould be causing water to not drain completely , that might lead to more problems in the future . I would also suggest fixing this faucet that isn ’ t shutting off properly . I could have it all finished by today if it ’ s urgent .\n\n[Turn 6] That would be great ! Is it expensive ?\n\n[Turn 7] Let ’ s see ... I would say about eight hundred dollars .\",\"[Turn 1] 下午好！是你叫的水管工吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，是的。请进！我真高兴你来了！这座老房子都要塌了！快去洗手间。看，这里，到处都在漏水！\n\n[Turn 3] 我知道了。让我看看。你的马桶好像堵住了，所以不能冲水。我去拿柱塞。不，那也不行。我怀疑管道里有异物导致堵塞。这就是你的马桶里的水溢出来的原因。\n\n[Turn 4] 哦，那一定是因为我四岁的女儿。她总是把东西扔进马桶。你知道孩子们是怎样的。\n\n[Turn 5] 是的，我也有个孩子。不管怎么说，这些水管真的生锈了，所以也应该换一下。这可能会导致水不能完全排出，之后还可能会导致更多的问题。我还建议你修理一下这个不能正常关闭的水龙头。如果你着急的话，我可以在今天之前把它们全部修好。\n\n[Turn 6] 那太好了！贵吗？\n\n[Turn 7] 让我看看……大约800美元吧。\",CONV_031,\nITEM_032,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 你好，哪里可以买到便宜的羊绒衫？\n\n[Turn 2] 也许你应该到处逛逛。\n\n[Turn 3] 这是个好主意。\n\n[Turn 4] 出口商店的价格更划算。\n\n[Turn 5] 谢谢你的帮助。\n\n[Turn 6] 不客气。祝你好运。\",\"[Turn 1] Hi, where can I buy a cheap cashmere sweater?\n\n[Turn 2] Maybe you should shop around.\n\n[Turn 3] That's a good idea.\n\n[Turn 4] The outlet stores have better prices.\n\n[Turn 5] Thanks for your help.\n\n[Turn 6] You're welcome. Good luck.\",CONV_032,\nITEM_033,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 很短很就是在。\n\n[Turn 2] 唉，上班期间对，不能，对，吊带是不允许穿的，然后。\n\n[Turn 3] 短短裙啊吊带啊。\n\n[Turn 4] 呃，那个很短的那个短裤啊，也也不要尽量不要穿。\n\n[Turn 5] 啊，那个短裙啊，就是只要。\",\"[Turn 1] Very short, just—yeah.\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah, during work hours, right, you can't—right, spaghetti straps aren't allowed, and then...\n\n[Turn 3] Short skirts, spaghetti straps.\n\n[Turn 4] Uh, those really short shorts, too—try not to wear those either.\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah, those short skirts, basically as long as...\",CONV_033,\nITEM_034,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我们正在找一位双语秘书。你认为你精通英语书面语和口语吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 我认为我的英语相当好。正如你从我的简历中看到的那样，我是以英语课程A等的成绩从大学毕业的。我系统地学习了英语语言学和英语文学。\n\n[Turn 3] 你的打字和速记技能如何？\n\n[Turn 4] 我一分钟能打80个字，并且基本上没有错，也能以每分钟120字的速度进行英语听写。\",\"[Turn 1] We are looking for a bilingual secretary . Do you think you are proficient in both written and spoken English ?\n\n[Turn 2] I think my English is fairly good . As you can see from my CV , I graduated from university with a B . A . degree in English . I studied the English language and English literature systematically .\n\n[Turn 3] How are your typing and shorthand skills ?\n\n[Turn 4] I can type 80 words a minute , basically no mistake , and can take dictation in English at 120 words per minute .\",CONV_034,\nITEM_035,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我收到你的通知，得知你已经把会计一职给了别人。我可以问一下为什么我落选了吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 我们仔细地考虑过你，但另一位候选人经验更丰富。\n\n[Turn 3] 经验很重要，但你不认为能力比经验更有价值吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 嗯，我想是的。但你如何向我证明你更有能力？\n\n[Turn 5] 也许你可以给我一次试用机会。如果我不能胜任这份工作，你可以解雇我。\n\n[Turn 6] 好主意。\",\"[Turn 1] I have just received your note which informs me that you have offered the accountant position to another candidate . May I ask why I was defeated ?\n\n[Turn 2] We have thought of you carefully with discretion , but the other candidate has more experiences .\n\n[Turn 3] Experience is important , but don't you think capability is more valuable than that ?\n\n[Turn 4] Yes , I think so . But how do you prove to me that you are more capable ?\n\n[Turn 5] Maybe you can hire me on trial . If I'm not qualified for the job , you can let me go .\n\n[Turn 6] Good idea .\",CONV_035,\nITEM_036,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Isn't it wonderful walking here ?\n\n[Turn 2] What do you mean ?\n\n[Turn 3] I mean look at all these magnificent buildings around us .\n\n[Turn 4] Yes , look over there . That's the Empire State Building . My book says it's 102 stories tall .\n\n[Turn 5] It's quite famous but don't you think it looks a bit old-fashioned ?\n\n[Turn 6] You're right , but when it was built in 1930 it was a marvel of technology and engineering .\n\n[Turn 7] What other important buildings are we going to see on Fifth Avenue ?\n\n[Turn 8] Quite a number . Actually every skyscraper has a history . A few blocks ahead we'll see St.Patrick ' s Cathedral and just across the street will be the world-renowed Rockefeller Center . It's a landmark in the history of architecture .\n\n[Turn 9] What's there after that ?\n\n[Turn 10] Well then , there's a Central Park . Facing the park on Fifth Avenue is probably some of the most expensive properties in the world .\n\n[Turn 11] What are they all for ?\n\n[Turn 12] Most of them are office buildings , huge department stores , and hotels but some are just private homes . New York is one of the financial centers of the world . And there are lots of very expensive places .\",\"[Turn 1] 在这儿走走，感觉真不错吧？\n\n[Turn 2] 你指什么？\n\n[Turn 3] 我是说，你看我们周围这些宏伟的建筑。\n\n[Turn 4] 是啊，看那边。那就是帝国大厦。我的书上说它有102层高。\n\n[Turn 5] 它挺有名的，不过你不觉得它看起来有点老派吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 你说得对，不过它在1930年建成的时候，可是科技和工程上的奇迹。\n\n[Turn 7] 在第五大道上，我们还会看到哪些重要的建筑？\n\n[Turn 8] 还挺多的。其实每一栋摩天大楼都有自己的历史。再往前走几个街区，我们会看到圣帕特里克大教堂，街对面就是世界闻名的洛克菲勒中心。它是建筑史上的一个地标。\n\n[Turn 9] 那之后还有什么？\n\n[Turn 10] 嗯，然后就是中央公园。第五大道上那些面向公园的房产，可能是世界上最贵的一些了。\n\n[Turn 11] 这些地方都是做什么用的？\n\n[Turn 12] 大多数是办公楼、大型百货商店和酒店，不过也有一些只是私人住宅。纽约是世界金融中心之一，也有很多特别昂贵的地方。\",CONV_036,\nITEM_037,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Good morning , sir . May I help you ?\n\n[Turn 2] Good morning , I have an appointment with Mr . Johnson at 10:00\n\n[Turn 3] Excuse me , sir , but are you Mr . Richard of World Trading Company ?\n\n[Turn 4] Yes . That ’ s right .\n\n[Turn 5] I ’ m sorry , Mr . Richard . Mr . Johnson is on his way to the office . He had just called and asked you to wait a minute .\n\n[Turn 6] Well , I ’ ll wait .\n\n[Turn 7] Would you like something to drink , sir ? Do you prefer coffee or tea ?\n\n[Turn 8] Thank you . Coffee , please .\n\n[Turn 9] Here you are , Mr . Richard . This is the cream and this is the sugar . If there ’ s anything else you ’ d like , please don ’ t hesitate to tell me .\n\n[Turn 10] Thank you very much .\",\"[Turn 1] 早上好，先生。有什么可以帮您的吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 早上好，我跟 Johnson 先生约了十点见面。\n\n[Turn 3] 不好意思，先生，请问您是 World Trading Company 的 Richard 先生吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 是的，没错。\n\n[Turn 5] 很抱歉，Richard 先生。Johnson 先生正在来办公室的路上。他刚刚打电话来，请您稍等一下。\n\n[Turn 6] 好的，我等一会儿。\n\n[Turn 7] 先生，您要喝点什么吗？咖啡还是茶？\n\n[Turn 8] 谢谢，请给我咖啡。\n\n[Turn 9] Richard 先生，给您。这是奶精，这是糖。您要是还需要什么，请随时告诉我。\n\n[Turn 10] 非常感谢。\",CONV_037,\nITEM_038,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 这个产品的卖点是技术先进。\n\n[Turn 2] 但是，它太贵了，大多数消费者都买不起。\n\n[Turn 3] 为什么价格这么高？\n\n[Turn 4] 不仅价格高，更新整个计算机系统使其兼容也要花很多钱。\n\n[Turn 5] 它和电脑不兼容？\n\n[Turn 6] 目前大多数计算机系统根本无法运行它，因为该产品确实性能太强了。\n\n[Turn 7] 或许在下一代技术问世后，这款车型的价格会变得更加实惠。\n\n[Turn 8] 但到那时，这项技术将会过时。\n\n[Turn 9] 没错，但我们的重点从来都不是经济承受能力。在沿海地区，我们可能不是很有竞争力，但质量方面，我们肯定有优势。\n\n[Turn 10] 没错，现在市场上没有其他产品可以相提并论。\n\n[Turn 11] 该机型技术先进，零部件精良，结构紧凑，是一款高品质的产品。\n\n[Turn 12] 你的努力会得到回报的。\",\"[Turn 1] The product's selling points is its advanced technoledge .\n\n[Turn 2] Unfortunately , it's just too expensive for majority of consumer to afford .\n\n[Turn 3] Why is the price so high ?\n\n[Turn 4] It's not just that the price is high , it's that the overhead to update an entire computer system to be compatible is costly .\n\n[Turn 5] Model of computers aren't compatible ?\n\n[Turn 6] Most current computer systems simply can't handle it because this model truly has extraordinary capabilities .\n\n[Turn 7] Maybe after the next generation of technology comes out , the price of this model will become more affordable .\n\n[Turn 8] But by then , the technology will be outdated .\n\n[Turn 9] True , but our focus has never been affordability anyway . Coastwise , we may not be very competitive , but qualitywise , we definitely have an edge .\n\n[Turn 10] That's right , no one else has a product on the market now that is comparable .\n\n[Turn 11] This model has advanced technoledge , superior components , it is compact , and it's a top-quality product .\n\n[Turn 12] I guess you get what you pay for .\",CONV_038,\nITEM_039,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Hey Sarah, I'm thinking about making a new dish for dinner tonight. Do you have any ideas?\n\n[Turn 2] Well, what are you in the mood for?\n\n[Turn 3] I'm not really sure. Something different, I guess.\n\n[Turn 4] Okay, well let me look through some recipes online and see what I can find.\n\n[Turn 5] Sounds good to me. Thanks, Sarah!\n\n[Turn 6] No problem. Let me know if you need any help with the cooking.\",\"[Turn 1] 嘿，Sarah，我在想今晚做道新菜当晚饭。你有什么主意吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，你想吃点什么口味的？\n\n[Turn 3] 我也不太确定。大概想吃点不一样的吧。\n\n[Turn 4] 好，那我上网翻翻菜谱，看看能找到什么。\n\n[Turn 5] 听起来不错。谢谢你，Sarah！\n\n[Turn 6] 没事。做饭的时候要是需要帮忙，就跟我说。\",CONV_039,\nITEM_040,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我很奇怪你们现场有这么几个人。你们有多种商品和业务，但是你们劳动力很少。\n\n[Turn 2] 这要根据一年中的不同时间的情况确定。在繁忙的时候我们招一些临时工帮着包装和装运。一年当中我们也把我们的一些业务包出去，比如，清洁工作。我们管理的非常严格！\n\n[Turn 3] 你们自己处理招聘业务吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 有时候我们靠当地的职业介绍所招人。那要看具体是什么工作。\",\"[Turn 1] I was surprised to see how few people you have on-site . You provide a wide range of goods and services but have a very small workforce .\n\n[Turn 2] It depends on the time of year . At peak times we hire in casual workers to help with packing and dispatch . We also contract out certain services all year round , for example , cleaning . We run a very tight operation !\n\n[Turn 3] Do you handle the recruiting yourselves ?\n\n[Turn 4] Sometimes we use a local employment agency . It depends on the job .\",CONV_040,\nITEM_041,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 对这样的话，我们就能够进入到你们学生那一块，就是能够更好的了解他们，对对对。\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，是更好的了解一下。\n\n[Turn 3] 嗯然后就像我们的话。\n\n[Turn 4] 就是关于。\",\"[Turn 1] That way, we'd be able to get into the student side of things on your end, and get a better understanding of them. Yeah, exactly.\n\n[Turn 2] Mm-hmm, just get a better understanding.\n\n[Turn 3] Mm-hmm, and then, for us...\n\n[Turn 4] It's about...\",CONV_041,\nITEM_042,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] using get measure .\n\n[Turn 2] Okay , yeah . The one where we current\n\n[Turn 3] So you know how zero is T_F_I_D_F_ . One is um the [disfmarker:] well I've called it word importance , but that's a really m misleading name .\n\n[Turn 4] Yeah . Yeah . Yeah . You know what , if you can [disfmarker:] if you introduce um like a sort of a static , what's it called , public static int . So basically a constant like that's Java's type of a constant , and give them names , like so zero T_D_I_D_F_ , one [disfmarker:] that probably makes the code a lot more readable for everybody who's playing around with it . You know you know what I mean ? So just like whatever , three means agreement value , and then I'd just write something agreement , and then it's easier to understand for both of us what's going on .\n\n[Turn 5] Yeah , probably .\n\n[Turn 6] Mm-hmm .\",\"[Turn 1] 用 get measure。\n\n[Turn 2] 好，对。就是我们现在用的那个……\n\n[Turn 3] 所以你知道，0 是 T_F_I_D_F_。1 是呃，那个——我叫它词重要性，但这个名字其实特别误导人。\n\n[Turn 4] 对，对，对。你知道吗，如果你能——如果你加一个那种静态的，叫什么来着，public static int。基本上就是一个常量，像 Java 里那种常量，然后给它们起名字，比如 0 是 T_D_I_D_F_，1 是——这样可能会让代码对所有拿来改的人都更好读。你懂我意思吧？比如随便说，3 代表一致值，那我就写个跟 agreement 有关的东西，这样我们俩都更容易看懂到底怎么回事。\n\n[Turn 5] 嗯，可能吧。\n\n[Turn 6] 嗯哼。\",CONV_042,\nITEM_043,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] \"\"Thank you so much for taking the time to meet with me today, it's really appreciated. I'm excited to share my portfolio with you and hopefully get a chance to work with you in the future.\"\"\n\n[Turn 2] \"\"Absolutely, it's always good to see new talent. And your portfolio is very impressive. I particularly like your black-and-white nature photos. There's something about the simplicity of them that really catches the eye.\"\"\n\n[Turn 3] \"\"Thank you, I'm glad you enjoy them. I actually took all of those photos within a year, and I feel like they really capture different aspects of nature. The light and shadows in particular were something I was trying to focus on.\"\"\n\n[Turn 4] \"\"That definitely comes through in your work. And your animal photos are also great. It's clear that you have a real passion for photography.\"\"\n\n[Turn 5] \"\"Absolutely, I've always loved taking photos of animals. I feel like they're so photogenic and there's always something new to capture. I'm actually hoping to do more work with animals in the future.\"\"\n\n[Turn 6] \"\"Well, we might be able to help you with that. We're always looking for talented photographers to work with us on our animal rescue projects. We think your work would be a great fit.\"\"\n\n[Turn 7] \"\"Thank you so much, I would love to work with you on that.\"\"\",\"[Turn 1] “非常感谢您今天抽时间跟我见面，我真的很感激。很高兴能把我的作品集分享给您，也希望以后有机会能和您合作。”\n\n[Turn 2] “当然，我们一直都很乐意看到新的摄影人才。而且你的作品集非常出色。我尤其喜欢你那些黑白的自然摄影作品，那种简洁感特别抓人眼球。”\n\n[Turn 3] “谢谢您，很高兴您喜欢。其实那些照片都是我在一年内拍的，我觉得它们确实捕捉到了大自然不同的面貌。尤其是光影部分，是我当时特别想去突出的。”\n\n[Turn 4] “这一点在你的作品里确实很明显。还有你的动物照片也很棒。看得出来，你对摄影真的很有热情。”\n\n[Turn 5] “是的，我一直都很喜欢拍动物。我觉得它们特别上镜，而且总能拍到新的东西。其实我也希望以后能更多地拍动物相关的项目。”\n\n[Turn 6] “嗯，这方面我们也许能帮上忙。我们一直在寻找有才华的摄影师，和我们一起参与动物救援项目。我们觉得你的作品会非常合适。”\n\n[Turn 7] “太感谢您了，我非常愿意和您一起做这个项目。”\",CONV_043,\nITEM_044,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Did you already take the history exam ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah . It was hard . When do you take it ?\n\n[Turn 3] I take it tomorrow morning . There is so much material that I dont know what to emphasize on . What types of questions did you get ?\n\n[Turn 4] Mostly on the civil war . You should also study the impact Martin Luther King Jr . had on American society .\n\n[Turn 5] What about Abraham Lincoln ? Did you get any questions about him ?\n\n[Turn 6] I only had 1 question about him . But you might get more . I dont know if he will have the same exam or not .\n\n[Turn 7] Hopefully he will use the same exam , cause Im going to spend most of my time studying the civil war . It is a huge section and that is what he lectured the most on in class .\n\n[Turn 8] If you cant study everything , then that is probably the best way to go .\n\n[Turn 9] Aright . Thanks for the info . I gotta go to the library now .\n\n[Turn 10] Good luck .\n\n[Turn 11] Thanks . See ya .\",\"[Turn 1] 你历史考试已经考完了吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，考完了。挺难的。你什么时候考？\n\n[Turn 3] 我明天早上考。内容太多了，我都不知道该重点看什么。你考到什么类型的题了？\n\n[Turn 4] 主要是关于南北战争的。你也应该复习一下马丁·路德·金对美国社会的影响。\n\n[Turn 5] 那亚伯拉罕·林肯呢？有考到他的题吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 我只有一道关于他的题。不过你可能会考到更多。我也不知道老师会不会用同一套卷子。\n\n[Turn 7] 希望他会用同一套吧，因为我打算把大部分时间都用来复习南北战争。那部分内容很多，而且也是他上课讲得最多的。\n\n[Turn 8] 如果你没法全都复习，那这样应该是最好的选择。\n\n[Turn 9] 好吧。谢谢你告诉我这些。我现在得去图书馆了。\n\n[Turn 10] 祝你好运。\n\n[Turn 11] 谢啦。回头见。\",CONV_044,\nITEM_045,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 你能帮我上网查一下吗\n\n[Turn 2] 当然可以。你想找到什么\n\n[Turn 3] 我想找到关于美国内战的信息\n\n[Turn 4] 呃，你能说得更具体些吗？有很多关于这方面的网站。\n\n[Turn 5] 是的，我想知道葛底斯堡战役。\n\n[Turn 6] 好的，（你可以）登陆google.com，输入“葛底斯堡战役”\n\n[Turn 7] 哇，网站太多了。\n\n[Turn 8] 来，试试这个。这是一个关于葛底斯堡的好网站。\n\n[Turn 9] 谢谢\n\n[Turn 10] 但是，要了解详细信息，你应该读一本历史书。\n\n[Turn 11] 谢谢。如果我感兴趣，我就去图书馆。\",\"[Turn 1] Can you help me look something up online?\n\n[Turn 2] Sure. What are you trying to find?\n\n[Turn 3] I want to find information about the American Civil War.\n\n[Turn 4] Uh, can you be more specific? There are a lot of websites about that.\n\n[Turn 5] Yes, I want to know about the Battle of Gettysburg.\n\n[Turn 6] Okay, go to google.com and type in “Battle of Gettysburg.”\n\n[Turn 7] Wow, there are so many websites.\n\n[Turn 8] Here, try this one. It’s a good website about Gettysburg.\n\n[Turn 9] Thanks.\n\n[Turn 10] But if you want detailed information, you should read a history book.\n\n[Turn 11] Thanks. If I’m interested, I’ll go to the library.\",CONV_045,\nITEM_046,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] You guys are charging me $ 10 for a movie that I never ordered or saw .\n\n[Turn 2] Let's see , sir . According to your file , you watched ' Titanic ' Monday evening .\n\n[Turn 3] Well , the wrong information is in my file . I was at a concert Monday night .\n\n[Turn 4] Well , your word overrules the file , sir . One moment , please .\n\n[Turn 5] I knew you'd see it my way .\n\n[Turn 6] Sir , I deleted the $ 10 , but I had to add a $ 2 service charge to your bill .\n\n[Turn 7] Am I in the Twilight Zone ? You're charging me for a movie I never saw ?\n\n[Turn 8] Please don't blame me , sir . Blame the computer programmer .\n\n[Turn 9] This is highway robbery . I've got a good mind to call the police !\n\n[Turn 10] If it makes you feel any better , other guests feel the same way .\",\"[Turn 1] 你们因为一部我从没订过或看过的电影收了我10美元。\n\n[Turn 2] 我看看，先生。根据你的档案，你周一晚上看了《泰坦尼克号》。\n\n[Turn 3] 嗯，我的档案里有错误的信息。我星期一晚上去听音乐会了。\n\n[Turn 4] 你的话能够更改档案，先生。请稍等。\n\n[Turn 5] 我知道你会按我的方式来做的。\n\n[Turn 6] 先生，我删除了那10美元，但我需要在您的账单上加上2美元的服务费。\n\n[Turn 7] 我在衰败地区吗？你要为一部我从没看过的电影向我收费？\n\n[Turn 8] 请不要怪我，先生。这得怪电脑程序员。\n\n[Turn 9] 这是高速公路抢劫。我很想报警！\n\n[Turn 10] 如果这能让你感觉好些，其他客人也会有同样的感觉。\",CONV_046,\nITEM_047,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Couple time .\n\n[Turn 2] Oh , great .\n\n[Turn 3] Well , I've done some research again about trends on the internet .\n\n[Turn 4] Um I've done some investigation , and uh well\n\n[Turn 5] I uh got some information from fashion watchers from Paris and uh Milan .\",\"[Turn 1] 情侣时间。\n\n[Turn 2] 哦，太好了。\n\n[Turn 3] 嗯，我又在网上查了一些趋势。\n\n[Turn 4] 嗯，我做了点调查，然后，呃……\n\n[Turn 5] 我，呃，从巴黎和米兰的一些时尚观察人士那儿弄到了一些信息。\",CONV_047,\nITEM_048,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Have heard of Paul ?\n\n[Turn 2] No , what ?\n\n[Turn 3] He's got a promotion .\n\n[Turn 4] You're kidding .\n\n[Turn 5] No , they made him vicepresident in charge of sells .\n\n[Turn 6] I don't believe it.He is only being with the company for two years .\n\n[Turn 7] Well , it's true.The board man last thirdly and they choice Paul .\n\n[Turn 8] Well.Good for him .\",\"[Turn 1] 你听说过保罗的事吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 没有，怎么了？\n\n[Turn 3] 他升职了。\n\n[Turn 4] 你开玩笑吧。\n\n[Turn 5] 不，他们让他当副总裁，负责销售。\n\n[Turn 6] 我不相信。他才在公司工作两年。\n\n[Turn 7] 嗯，这是真的。董事会成员选择了保罗。\n\n[Turn 8] 好吧。对他而言，这是件好事。\",CONV_048,\nITEM_049,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 所以你看看。\n\n[Turn 2] 你们看看。\n\n[Turn 3] 哪几个版块你们觉得。\n\n[Turn 4] 三个板块，告诉他们我们最想改进的。\n\n[Turn 5] 让他们去加到这份调研问卷里去。\n\n[Turn 6] 我觉得这个肯定是下载了。\n\n[Turn 7] 都没下载根本就，根本就不可能有以下的所有的板块了。\n\n[Turn 8] 所以我觉得下载。\",\"[Turn 1] So take a look.\n\n[Turn 2] All of you, have a look.\n\n[Turn 3] Which sections do you think...\n\n[Turn 4] Pick three sections and tell them the ones we most want to improve.\n\n[Turn 5] Have them add those to this survey questionnaire.\n\n[Turn 6] I think downloads are definitely one.\n\n[Turn 7] If people haven't even downloaded it, then there's no way they'll get to any of the sections after that.\n\n[Turn 8] So yeah, I think downloads.\",CONV_049,\nITEM_050,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Do you have anything to do after this ?\n\n[Turn 2] No , I don't .\n\n[Turn 3] Shall we drop in somewhere for a couple of drinks ?\n\n[Turn 4] That sounds like a good idea .\n\n[Turn 5] I know a very interesting place .\n\n[Turn 6] Oh , do you ? Good .\",\"[Turn 1] 这之后你还有什么事吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 没有，我没事。\n\n[Turn 3] 那我们找个地方去喝两杯怎么样？\n\n[Turn 4] 听起来不错。\n\n[Turn 5] 我知道一个挺有意思的地方。\n\n[Turn 6] 哦，是吗？太好了。\",CONV_050,\nITEM_051,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 好的，跟我聊聊你自己吧。\n\n[Turn 2] 格林先生，你想知道什么？\n\n[Turn 3] 你有什么工作经验\n\n[Turn 4] 2004年，我在广州附近的一家贸易公司的销售部找到了一份工作。我开始做销售代表。一年后，我被提升为销售经理。从那以后，我一直做那份工作，到现在才一年多。\n\n[Turn 5] 哦，很好。艾琳，你能告诉我你为什么打算辞去销售经理的工作到这里来做我的助理吗？你不喜欢你现在的工作吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 坦白说，我很喜欢其中的一部分，但我更喜欢更专业的工作。碰巧我有个朋友在这家公司工作。她告诉我出口部要招聘一名助理。听到这个消息我感到非常兴奋。所以我才来这里。\",\"[Turn 1] All right, tell me a little about yourself.\n\n[Turn 2] What would you like to know, Mr. Green?\n\n[Turn 3] What kind of work experience do you have?\n\n[Turn 4] In 2004, I got a job in the sales department of a trading company near Guangzhou. I started out as a sales representative. A year later, I was promoted to sales manager. I've been doing that job ever since, so it's been just over a year now.\n\n[Turn 5] Oh, very good. Irene, can you tell me why you're planning to leave your sales manager position and come here to be my assistant? Don't you like your current job?\n\n[Turn 6] To be honest, I do like parts of it, but I'd prefer something more professional. As it happens, I have a friend who works at this company. She told me the export department was looking to hire an assistant. I was really excited when I heard that. That's why I'm here.\",CONV_051,\nITEM_052,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我们是继续在那边搞个什么。\n\n[Turn 2] 晚会呀，还是就是。\n\n[Turn 3] 接回来，出门去KTV开始高兴下，还是就直接回去，你觉得这个。\n\n[Turn 4] 晚上，就是再组织下娱乐活动。\n\n[Turn 5] 咳，那边晚会的话，我我想，我我了解了一下，那边三圣乡团建。\n\n[Turn 6] 晚会的话那边好像是没什么晚会，都是。\n\n[Turn 7] 都好像都是大家吃完饭吃到下午吃到下午饭嘛，然后就回来了嘛。\",\"[Turn 1] Should we keep doing something over there?\n\n[Turn 2] Like a party, or just...\n\n[Turn 3] Come back, then go out to KTV and have some fun, or just go straight back? What do you think?\n\n[Turn 4] In the evening, I mean, maybe organize some more entertainment.\n\n[Turn 5] Ahem, if we're talking about a party over there, I, I was thinking, I, I asked around about team building in Sanshengxiang.\n\n[Turn 6] As for a party, it seems like they don't really have anything like that over there. It's all...\n\n[Turn 7] It seems like everyone just eats after they finish dinner, keeps eating into the afternoon, has the afternoon meal, and then comes back.\",CONV_052,\nITEM_053,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Hey, babe. How are you doing today?\n\n[Turn 2] I'm doing alright. How are you?\n\n[Turn 3] I'm good. Just wanted to check in with you and see how your day is going.\n\n[Turn 4] It's going well. I just finished up my classes for the day and now I'm headed home.\n\n[Turn 5] That sounds great. I'll see you soon then.\n\n[Turn 6] Yep, see you soon!\",\"[Turn 1] 嘿，宝贝。你今天怎么样？\n\n[Turn 2] 我还行。你呢？\n\n[Turn 3] 我挺好的。就是想问问你，看看你今天过得怎么样。\n\n[Turn 4] 挺顺利的。我今天的课刚上完，现在正往家走。\n\n[Turn 5] 那挺好。那我一会儿见。\n\n[Turn 6] 嗯，一会儿见！\",CONV_053,\nITEM_054,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Ann , do you have time next Monday ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah , what ’ s up ?\n\n[Turn 3] Next Monday is my birthday , and I would like you to attend my party .\n\n[Turn 4] Wow . I'd love to .\n\n[Turn 5] Great !\n\n[Turn 6] When and where ?\n\n[Turn 7] Five o ’ clock that afternoon , and in my place , you know ?\n\n[Turn 8] Yes , I know . I appreciate your invitation .\n\n[Turn 9] I am going to invite other guys . See you that day .\n\n[Turn 10] See you .\",\"[Turn 1] Ann，你下周一有空吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 有啊，怎么了？\n\n[Turn 3] 下周一是我生日，我想请你来参加我的派对。\n\n[Turn 4] 哇，我很乐意去。\n\n[Turn 5] 太好了！\n\n[Turn 6] 什么时候，在哪儿？\n\n[Turn 7] 那天下午五点，在我家，你知道的吧？\n\n[Turn 8] 嗯，我知道。谢谢你的邀请。\n\n[Turn 9] 我还要去邀请其他人。那天见。\n\n[Turn 10] 到时候见。\",CONV_054,\nITEM_055,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] You have been here for how long ? Four months now ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yeah , about .\n\n[Turn 3] Do you know Chinese better now ?\n\n[Turn 4] Oh , definitely . I remember , when I first arrived in Guangzhou , my girlfriend was haggling with a sales clerk over the price of a mobile phone .\n\n[Turn 5] Oh , yeah . Many Chinese like to bargain . It happens almost everywhere .\n\n[Turn 6] I mean , I understand that . But the speed of the conversation got faster and faster , until it seemed to me that they would fight . My perception of the tone was that it was a violent shouting match . The truth was that it was a perfectly normal conversation .\n\n[Turn 7] A shouting match ? You ’ re so funny . You must be exaggerating . I don ’ t believe it .\n\n[Turn 8] I am not exaggerating at all . I ’ m telling you the truth . That was how I felt at that time .\n\n[Turn 9] Yes , perhaps . Chinese usually don ’ t notice that sort of thing . Maybe it ’ s quite natural to us .\n\n[Turn 10] Yes , absolutely true .\",\"[Turn 1] 你在这里多久了？四个月了？\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，大概。\n\n[Turn 3] 你现在中文好些了吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 哦，当然。我记得，刚到广州的时候，我女朋友和一个售货员就一部手机还价。\n\n[Turn 5] 哦，是的。许多中国人喜欢还价。它几乎无处不在。\n\n[Turn 6] 我明白。但是他们说话的速度越来越快，我都觉得他们会打架。我觉得这是一场激烈的叫喊比赛。但事实是，这是一次非常正常的谈话。\n\n[Turn 7] 叫喊比赛？你真有趣。你一定是夸大了。我不相信。\n\n[Turn 8] 我一点也没夸大。我说的是实话。那就是我当时的感受。\n\n[Turn 9] 好吧，也许吧。中国人通常不会注意到这种事情。也许这对我们来说很自然。\n\n[Turn 10] 是的，就是这样。\",CONV_055,\nITEM_056,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 请告诉我根据相关的规定我要怎样把这些文件归档。\n\n[Turn 2] 好的，没问题。当你把文件，资料或其它东西归档时，有四点你应该记在心上。\n\n[Turn 3] 什么？\n\n[Turn 4] 它们是：按时间先后顺序排好这些文件，去掉所有的碎片和大头针，将文件对齐订好，然后放进文件夹。\n\n[Turn 5] 最重要的一点是什么？\n\n[Turn 6] 你必须牢记每个客户都要存档。\",\"[Turn 1] Please tell me how to file things according to the concerned rules .\n\n[Turn 2] Well , all right . There are four points you should keep in mind when you file documents , information and other things .\n\n[Turn 3] What are they ?\n\n[Turn 4] They are keep the documents in chronological order , remove all the chips and pins , punch the documents evenly and place them in the folder .\n\n[Turn 5] And what is the most important point ?\n\n[Turn 6] You should always remember that one customer one file is the rule .\",CONV_056,\nITEM_057,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] OK , everyone . Gather around . Here are the rules . No tackling . No pushing .\n\n[Turn 2] You shouldn't grab someone else's shirt . That's a foul .\n\n[Turn 3] Play is stopped when the person with the ball is touched .\n\n[Turn 4] You can touch them only between the shoulder and the knees .\n\n[Turn 5] The touchdown lines are there and there . OK , let's play !\n\n[Turn 6] Before we start , let's have a moment of silence for our fallen men .\",\"[Turn 1] 好了，各位，过来集合。我来说一下规则：不许抱摔，不许推人。\n\n[Turn 2] 不能拽别人的球衣，那是犯规。\n\n[Turn 3] 持球的人一被碰到，比赛就暂停。\n\n[Turn 4] 只能碰他们肩膀到膝盖之间的位置。\n\n[Turn 5] 达阵线在那边，还有那边。好了，开打吧！\n\n[Turn 6] 开始之前，我们先为牺牲的弟兄们默哀片刻。\",CONV_057,\nITEM_058,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] It's the latest and quite popular among young people .\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , I know and I like it very much . I will take it .\n\n[Turn 3] Sure . Here is your receipt .\n\n[Turn 4] How long is this cell phone guaranteed ?\n\n[Turn 5] You can refund it in 7 days and exchange it in one year .\",\"[Turn 1] 这是最新款，在年轻人中很流行。\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，我知道，我非常喜欢。我要了。\n\n[Turn 3] 好的。这是您的收据。\n\n[Turn 4] 这部手机保修期多久？\n\n[Turn 5] 您可以在7天内退货，一年内换货。\",CONV_058,\nITEM_059,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Good afternoon . Can I help you ?\n\n[Turn 2] I need some remedies for an upset stomach .\n\n[Turn 3] Are you also suffering from pain and fever ?\n\n[Turn 4] Yes , and I also have the runs\n\n[Turn 5] I'll give you some tablets that should make you feel better . One moment , please . Here you are . Take these tablets three times a day swallow them with water .\n\n[Turn 6] When should I take them ?\n\n[Turn 7] Take on after each meal .\n\n[Turn 8] How long should I continue taking them ?\n\n[Turn 9] Take them for two days.If your symptoms persist for more than two days , you should see a doctor Also , be sure to drink plenty of water to prevent dehydration .\n\n[Turn 10] Thank you for your advice .\",\"[Turn 1] 下午好，有什么可以帮您的？\n\n[Turn 2] 我需要一些治疗胃痛的药物\n\n[Turn 3] 有疼痛和发烧的症状么？\n\n[Turn 4] 是的，我现在还拉肚子。\n\n[Turn 5] 我给您开一些药，这些药可以让您感觉舒眼点。请稍等。给您药。一天吃三次，白水送服。\n\n[Turn 6] 我应该什么时候吃？\n\n[Turn 7] 饭后吃一片。\n\n[Turn 8] 我要吃多久？\n\n[Turn 9] 吃两天。如果两天之后仍不见好转，您就应该去看医生。而且，一定要多喝水，以免脱水。\n\n[Turn 10] 谢谢你的建议。\",CONV_059,\nITEM_060,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] So hank you very much .\n\n[Turn 2] Thank you .\n\n[Turn 3] And we'll see you after lunch .\",\"[Turn 1] 那就非常感谢你。\n\n[Turn 2] 谢谢。\n\n[Turn 3] 那我们午饭后见。\",CONV_060,\nITEM_061,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] I ’ d like to apply for a personal loan .\n\n[Turn 2] How much would you like to borrow ?\n\n[Turn 3] A thousand dollars .\n\n[Turn 4] Let me check with a credit manager . A record show your credit reading is quite high . I don't think you have any problems .\n\n[Turn 5] What ’ s the current interest rate ?\n\n[Turn 6] Our monthly interest is 1.5 % of the outstanding balance . Would you please fill out the application the form ?\",\"[Turn 1] 我想申请个人贷款\n\n[Turn 2] 你想借多少钱？\n\n[Turn 3] 一千美元。\n\n[Turn 4] 让我和信贷经理核实一下。根据记录，您的信用分相当高，可以贷款。\n\n[Turn 5] 现在的利率是多少？\n\n[Turn 6] 我们的月利息是未清余额的1.5%。请填一下申请表好吗？\",CONV_061,\nITEM_062,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] So, I set you up on a date!\n\n[Turn 2] Oh, yeah? Who is it?\n\n[Turn 3] Her name is Sarah and she's really friendly. I think you'll like her.\n\n[Turn 4] Okay, cool. When are we going out?\n\n[Turn 5] Tomorrow night at 7.\n\n[Turn 6] Great, I'll look forward to it. Thanks for setting this up, Jlynn.\",\"[Turn 1] 所以，我给你安排了一场约会！\n\n[Turn 2] 哦，是吗？对方是谁？\n\n[Turn 3] 她叫 Sarah，人特别友好。我觉得你会喜欢她的。\n\n[Turn 4] 好啊，挺不错的。我们什么时候出去？\n\n[Turn 5] 明晚七点。\n\n[Turn 6] 太好了，我很期待。谢谢你帮我安排，Jlynn。\",CONV_062,\nITEM_063,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 我想买三张票。入场费是多少\n\n[Turn 2] 每人10美元\n\n[Turn 3] 这是30美元。顺便问一下，我在哪里可以找到导游？\n\n[Turn 4] 去下一个窗口，那里的人会帮你找到导游。\n\n[Turn 5] 非常感谢。\",\"[Turn 1] I'd like to buy three tickets. How much is admission?\n\n[Turn 2] It's 10 dollars per person.\n\n[Turn 3] Here's 30 dollars. By the way, where can I find a tour guide?\n\n[Turn 4] Go to the next window. The people there will help you find a guide.\n\n[Turn 5] Thank you very much.\",CONV_063,\nITEM_064,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] The stepmother was very wicked . She couldn't stand a happy smile on the boy's face .\n\n[Turn 2] And ?\n\n[Turn 3] And she did her best to pull out the thorn in her flesh and the boy lost whatever made him happy .\n\n[Turn 4] Poor child !\",\"[Turn 1] 这个继母特别恶毒。她最见不得那男孩脸上露出开心的笑容。\n\n[Turn 2] 然后呢？\n\n[Turn 3] 然后她想尽办法要拔掉这个眼中钉，害得那男孩失去了所有让他快乐的东西。\n\n[Turn 4] 可怜的孩子！\",CONV_064,\nITEM_065,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] And we'll need to custom desi design a circuit board , because the circuit board has to take the button input and send it to the output so you have to design that each time . But once we come up with a design we'll send it to the circuit people and they'll just print it out .\n\n[Turn 2] Um , standard parts include the buttons and the wheels , um the iPod-style wheel . The infrared L_E_D_ is actually gonna be included in the circuit board that comes with it . Um , we need a radio sender and receiver , those are standard . And al we also need a beeper or buzzer or other sort of noise thing for locating the remote .\n\n[Turn 3] So we have some material options . Um , we can use rubber , plastic , wood or titanium . Um , I'd recommend against titanium because it can only be used in the flat cases and it's really heavy . Um , and the rubber case requires rubber buttons , so if we definitely want plastic buttons , we shouldn't have a rubber case .\n\n[Turn 4] And why not wood ? And why not wood ? [vocalsound:laugh] [gap:] [vocalsound:laugh]\n\n[Turn 5] And , hmm ?\n\n[Turn 6] [vocalsound:laugh] Uh , well we can use wood . [vocalsound:laugh] I don't know why we'd want to . Um and also we should note that if we want an iPod-style wheel button , it's gonna require a m qu slightly more expensive chip . We can't use the minimal chip , we need the next higher grade , which is called regular . I don't think it's much more expensive , but it is more expensive .\n\n[Turn 7] So that's what I've got on design .\",\"[Turn 1] 然后我们还得专门设计一块电路板，因为电路板要接收按键输入，再把信号送到输出端，所以每次都得设计这个。不过一旦我们把方案定下来，就发给做电路板的人，他们直接印出来就行。\n\n[Turn 2] 嗯，标准零件包括按键和滚轮，嗯，就是 iPod 那种滚轮。红外 L_E_D_ 其实会集成在随附的那块电路板里。嗯，我们需要一个无线发射器和接收器，这些都是标准件。还有，我们还需要一个蜂鸣器、 buzzer，或者别的能发出声音的东西，用来找遥控器。\n\n[Turn 3] 所以材料方面有几个选择。嗯，我们可以用橡胶、塑料、木头或者钛。嗯，我不建议用钛，因为它只能用在平面外壳上，而且真的很重。嗯，另外橡胶外壳就得配橡胶按键，所以如果我们确定想要塑料按键，那就不该用橡胶外壳。\n\n[Turn 4] 那为什么不用木头？为什么不用木头？[vocalsound:laugh] [gap:] [vocalsound:laugh]\n\n[Turn 5] 还有，嗯？\n\n[Turn 6] [vocalsound:laugh] 呃，其实我们可以用木头。[vocalsound:laugh] 我只是不知道我们为什么会想用。嗯，另外还得注意，如果我们想要 iPod 那种滚轮按键，就需要一块嗯……稍微贵一点的芯片。不能用最低配的芯片，得用高一档的，叫 regular。我觉得也贵不了太多，但确实会更贵。\n\n[Turn 7] 所以设计方面，我这边就这些。\",CONV_065,\nITEM_066,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] Yeah , if [disfmarker:]\n\n[Turn 2] [gap:] Sorry . Yeah . Uh as you know , I am mister Ramaro . I am an expert in uh industrial design of all electronic devices and I previously devised many uh [disfmarker:] like digital calculators and electronic calculators . [vocalsound:other] So now I'll briefly describe the working design of our remote control .\n\n[Turn 3] You prefer it [gap:] . [vocalsound:laugh]\n\n[Turn 4] Well , as you know the basic function of remote control is sending some message to the the device , like T_V_ or V_C_R_ or D_V_D_ player etcetera .\n\n[Turn 5] So we will have a p portable device which will send message to the the main device like T_V_ .\n\n[Turn 6] So we need to have some energy source to do what [disfmarker:] to do the functions , what we want on this portable device . [vocalsound:other]\n\n[Turn 7] And usually this [disfmarker:] so to do these functions we need an interface , which basically some kind of pressing buttons or keys or like moving jack or something like that .\n\n[Turn 8] And then these messages [disfmarker:] these key buttons can be transferred into some kind of message and then it will process by the chip and then it will generate some information to the main device .\",\"[Turn 1] 对，如果[disfmarker:]\n\n[Turn 2] [gap:] 抱歉。对。呃，大家知道，我是Ramaro先生。我是，呃，各类电子设备工业设计方面的专家，之前也设计过很多，呃[disfmarker:] 比如数码计算器、电子计算器之类的。[vocalsound:other] 那现在我简单介绍一下我们这款遥控器的工作设计。\n\n[Turn 3] 你更喜欢它[gap:]。[vocalsound:laugh]\n\n[Turn 4] 嗯，大家也知道，遥控器最基本的功能，就是给设备发送一些信息，比如电视、VCR录像机、DVD播放器等等。\n\n[Turn 5] 所以我们会有一个便携式设备，用来给主要设备，比如电视，发送信息。\n\n[Turn 6] 所以我们需要有某种能量来源，来做什么[disfmarker:] 来在这个便携式设备上实现我们想要的那些功能。[vocalsound:other]\n\n[Turn 7] 而且通常这个[disfmarker:] 所以要实现这些功能，我们需要一个界面，基本上就是某种按按钮、按键，或者像移动操纵杆之类的东西。\n\n[Turn 8] 然后这些信息[disfmarker:] 这些按键按钮可以被转换成某种信息，然后由芯片处理，接着它会给主要设备生成一些信息。\",CONV_066,\nITEM_067,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 需要帮忙吗\n\n[Turn 2] 是的，我需要一些旅行支票。\n\n[Turn 3] 你需要多少钱？\n\n[Turn 4] 三千美元。\n\n[Turn 5] 好的，能给我你的存折吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 好的，给你。\n\n[Turn 7] 你需要哪个账户的支票？\n\n[Turn 8] 对我来说都一样。\n\n[Turn 9] 给你。\n\n[Turn 10] 谢谢\",\"[Turn 1] Can I help you ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , I need some traveler's checks .\n\n[Turn 3] How much do you need ?\n\n[Turn 4] Three thousand US dollars .\n\n[Turn 5] All right , can I have your passbook ?\n\n[Turn 6] Yes , here you go .\n\n[Turn 7] What amounts do you want the checks in ?\n\n[Turn 8] It's all the same to me .\n\n[Turn 9] Here you are .\n\n[Turn 10] Thanks .\",CONV_067,\nITEM_068,en-zh,\"[Turn 1] How silly of you to jump out of the window !\n\n[Turn 2] But that was the first thing that came into my mind when I heard the shout earthquake !\n\n[Turn 3] Why not use staircases ? The terror was not so violent at that time .\n\n[Turn 4] That would be too late .\n\n[Turn 5] Maybe the situation is too urgent .\n\n[Turn 6] Yes , I think I should have jumped in any case .\",\"[Turn 1] 你怎么这么傻，居然从窗户跳出去！\n\n[Turn 2] 可我一听到有人喊“地震”时，脑子里第一个想到的就是这个！\n\n[Turn 3] 为什么不走楼梯呢？当时还没到那么吓人的程度吧。\n\n[Turn 4] 那样就来不及了。\n\n[Turn 5] 可能情况太紧急了。\n\n[Turn 6] 是啊，我觉得不管怎样我都该跳的。\",CONV_068,\nITEM_069,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 有什么我能帮你的吗？\n\n[Turn 2] 我是安德森咨询公司的詹姆斯·梅森。我想见史密斯先生。\n\n[Turn 3] 你预约了吗？\n\n[Turn 4] 预约了，他知道我要来。我们的会议定在两点。\n\n[Turn 5] 我想史密斯先生可能忘记了这场会议。他今天早上离开了办公室，恐怕下午4点之后才能回来。让我看看他有没有安排其他人代他见你。请坐好吗？\n\n[Turn 6] 好的。\n\n[Turn 7] 好的，梅森先生，我刚和我们的办公室经理泰瑞女士谈过。她说，史密斯向她简要介绍了你的项目。她刚刚结束一个会议，很快就会过来见你。请稍等一下，要不要我带你四处看看？\n\n[Turn 8] 那太好了。非常感谢。\n\n[Turn 9] 这边请，梅森先生。我们可以从前厅开始看。泰瑞女士准备好了的时候，你就可以坐前面的电梯到6楼。会议室已经准备好了。\",\"[Turn 1] How can I help you ?\n\n[Turn 2] Yes , I am James Mason from Anderson and Associates . I would like to see Mr . Smith .\n\n[Turn 3] Do you have an appointment ?\n\n[Turn 4] Yes , he knows I'm coming . Our meeting is set for 2 o'clock .\n\n[Turn 5] I wonder if Mr . Smith forgot your meeting . I am afraid he left this office this morning and is not expected back until after 4 pm . Let me find out if he made arrangements for someone else to meet with you in his place . Will you please have a seat ?\n\n[Turn 6] Sure .\n\n[Turn 7] Yes , Mr . Mason , I just checked with our office manager , Ms . Terry , she said Mr . Smith briefed her on your project . She is just finishing up a meeting now . She could be with your shortly . Would you like me to show you around while you are waiting ?\n\n[Turn 8] That would be very nice . Thank you .\n\n[Turn 9] Right this way , Mr . Mason . We can start with our front office . When Ms . Terry is ready , you may take the elevator at the front to the 6th floor . There is a conference room already prepared\",CONV_069,\nITEM_070,zh-en,\"[Turn 1] 除非很好很贵重的杯子。\n\n[Turn 2] 保温杯啊，现在随便一个保温杯，不要两三百三四百啊。\",\"[Turn 1] Unless it's a really nice, expensive cup.\n\n[Turn 2] Like a thermos. These days, any random thermos can easily cost two or three hundred, even three or four hundred.\",CONV_070,\n";
